    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Doubling up on your prescribed medication to intensively treat an acute episode could be risky, because it might lead you to take more than what your body can safely handle. Overuse of medication can lead to serious health problems, including medication-overdose syndrome. Since I can't access your medical prescriptions or fully understand your medical history, it's strongly advised that you consult with a healthcare professional first. They can provide guidance based on your specific situation and ensure you're taking the correct treatment safely. It's okay to want to avoid an uncomfortable visit to the ER, but your safety and health should be the priority. Pain that occurs suddenly and feels much more intense than usual warrants professional medical evaluation, and they can help you understand if you need immediate care or can manage your symptoms at home safely. Remember, your peace of mind and well-being truly matter.",
